WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:00.838
Finish a painting with me!

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:03.461
We're painting with oil — let's put some final touches together.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.321
For red, I chose Rembrandt Permanent Red Deep, artist-quality oil paint.

4
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:13.866
Next goes Van Gogh Cadmium Yellow — a gorgeous non-transparent colour. I just love it.

5
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:21.853
As an addition, I'm using Winsor and Newton Fluorescent Yellow.

6
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:27.038
Look how bright it is — sick.

7
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.057
Next we have Rembrandt Turquoise — just a tiny bit as an addition.

8
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:38.326
Rembrandt Periwinkle. It's transparent, and I'm absolutely obsessed with it.

9
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:46.248
Looks almost like Pantone Veri Peri. Viridian hue as an addition to create the shadings.

10
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:54.861
I like to organise my work — paints in separate boxes so I know where to search for what I need.

11
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:05.612
I use scent-free turpentine as a medium.

12
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:11.910
And that's how the final touches come together.

13
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.058
Mad Mojo — art with a little madness in it.
